line	
line	<col=000080>Climb the watchtower in Glough's house (tree in the east part of his house). Use the sticks with the four pillars to spell out TUZO. If you are under 25 <col=800000>Agility</col>, eat your <col=800000>summer pie</col> now.</col>
step	21	-	Quick guide step 21
line	<str>Speak to King Shareen in the Grand Tree with two empty slots to receive a translation book and a bark sample.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Hazelmere in his house on the island east of Yanille (fairy ring code: CLS). He will take your bark sample and give you a message for the king.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to King Shareen. He will ask what the message says. Tell him:</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south. At the bottom of the incline, turn east and go up the ladder to speak with Glough.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to King Shareen, and he will tell you that Glough has caught a human. Ask to see the prisoner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the prisoner Charlie on the top floor of the Grand Tree. Make sure to finish the entire conversation!</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Glough's house. Search the cupboard, and you will find his journal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Glough and wait to be arrested.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Charlie; he will tell you about the shipyard on Karamja; the password is Ka-Lu-Min.</str>
line	
line	<str>The king appears and tells you to escape using the gnome glider on top of the tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel with the glider.</str>
line	
line	<str>The glider will crash near the Ship Yard. Run east past the level 53 jogres to the Ship Yard gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the gate and tell the worker Glough sent you, then give the password Ka-Lu-Min.</str>
line	
line	<str>Find the Foreman on the southern dock. Kill him or talk to him to get a lumber order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the lumber order to the king. (Teleport into the stronghold or get Femi to sneak you in, costing 1,000 coins if you didn't help her earlier). The king will not believe you when you show him the lumber order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Charlie again on the top floor of the Grand Tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Anita up the stairs west of the swamp, north-west of the Grand Tree. She will give you a key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Glough's house, and use the key to open the chest and take the invasion plans.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the invasion plans to the king. He will give you four letters made of sticks (you'll need 4 empty inventory spaces).</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb the watchtower in Glough's house (tree in the east part of his house). Use the sticks with the four pillars to spell out TUZO. If you are under 25 Agility, eat your summer pie now.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Bank if needed and prepare for the battle, then go down the trapdoor.</col>
